WAMR's ESP-IDF port: AOT code in PSRAM, mapped executable (the wasm probe; nothing in any build applies this)

Applies to: WAMR (github.com/wasm-micro-runtime/wasm-micro-runtime) tag WAMR-2.4.5,
commit 25bd7eb63e828e4bd242cc9b38d260b4b31c6605.
Licence: this is a modification of WAMR, so it is under WAMR's licence, Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception,
NOT the MIT licence of the rest of this repository.
Why and how it was measured: docs/wasm-probe.md ("The game's code in PSRAM, mapped executable").
Kept by abacus's ruling (#5169); whether it is carried or upstreamed waits on Michael's ruling.

What it changes:
- espidf_memmap.c: os_mmap(MMAP_PROT_EXEC) allocates page-aligned PSRAM and maps its physical pages
  executable with esp_mmu_map; os_get_dbus_mirror returns the block's data address; os_munmap unmaps.
  Replaces the fixed MEM_DUAL_BUS_OFFSET, which sends PSRAM 0x3C.. to 0x3A.. on the ESP32-S3.
- shared_platform.cmake: the dual-bus mirror on for CONFIG_SPIRAM (was CONFIG_ESP32S3_SPIRAM_SUPPORT).
- build-scripts/esp-idf/wamr/CMakeLists.txt: REQUIRES esp_mm esp_psram heap.
- aot_reloc_xtensa.c: a diagnostic print in check_reloc_offset's failure branch (the probe's
  instrument; not needed for the fix).

diff --git a/build-scripts/esp-idf/wamr/CMakeLists.txt b/build-scripts/esp-idf/wamr/CMakeLists.txt
index b47cd16..82000df 100644
